# large artifacts stay out of git (obtune convention): manifests, resolved configs and
# run_manifest.json files ARE committed; adapters, corpora, trials and caches are not.
data/
# runs/ and results/ now default to $BIDIR_OUT, OUTSIDE the working tree (docs/STORAGE.md).
# The rules stay so that a stray one written into the repo is still ignored rather than
# committed: the grid produces ~455 GB and none of it belongs in git. Real provenance lives in
# each adapter's run_manifest.json and each result's summary.json, which carry the git sha, the
# resolved config and the script hashes.
runs/
bidir_out/
results/
third_party/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.log

# papers/ IS committed: the literature this project positions against is part of the record,
# and a related-work claim that cannot be checked against the actual PDF is not a claim.
!papers/
!papers/*.pdf

# The draft PDF IS committed (56 KB): a collaborator should be able to read it without
# installing a TeX toolchain, and its unfilled numbers are visible on the page.
!paper/main.pdf
